skia-rust is licensed under the BSD-3-Clause licence (see LICENSE). It also contains
ports of third-party C libraries that Skia wraps. Each port is a separate crate with
its own licence file, and the upstream licence text is reproduced there unchanged.

| Library (pinned version)                                  | Ported as                | Licence       | Licence text                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------|---------------|--------------------------------------|
| zlib, Chromium fork 1.3.0.1-motley (646b7f56)             | skia-rust-zlib           | Zlib          | crates/skia-rust-zlib/LICENSE        |
| libpng 1.6.56                                             | skia-rust-libpng         | libpng-2.0    | crates/skia-rust-libpng/LICENSE      |
| libjpeg-turbo 3.1.0 (e14cbfaa)                            | skia-rust-libjpeg        | IJG, BSD-3-Clause, Zlib | crates/skia-rust-libjpeg/LICENSE |
| libwebp 1.4.0 (845d5476)                                  | skia-rust-libwebp        | BSD-3-Clause  | crates/skia-rust-libwebp/LICENSE     |
| Wuffs v0.3 (e3f919cc)                                     | skia-rust-wuffs          | Apache-2.0    | crates/skia-rust-wuffs/LICENSE       |

Wuffs (crates/skia-rust-wuffs) is Apache-2.0, not BSD. Its upstream copyright notice is
"Copyright 2017 The Wuffs Authors", and the Apache License, Version 2.0 text is reproduced
unchanged in crates/skia-rust-wuffs/LICENSE. skia-rust-wuffs is a modified version of Wuffs
(a Rust port of its GIF decoder, LZW and base modules); each of its source files carries the
upstream notice and states that it is modified, as Apache-2.0 section 4 requires.

The libjpeg-turbo pin is the commit `e14cbfaa85529d47f9f55b0f104a579c1061f9ad` of
`chromium/deps/libjpeg_turbo` that `third_party/skia/DEPS` names for m156. The C oracle
for `skia-rust-libjpeg` is built from that commit by `oracle/codec-diff/libjpeg/build.sh`.

A row whose crate is not yet in the workspace is a planned port (docs/design/codecs.md
§3); its licence file is added with the crate. The Rust-backed codecs Skia can use
(png, zune-jpeg, jpeg-encoder) are dependencies, not ports, and are listed in Cargo.lock.
